    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "p∗i∗0(i∗1bJ + δϕ) = δv. Note that i∗1bJ +δϕ is a bounded cocycle on G. Since v is a bounded function, the second bounded cohomology class p∗i∗0[i∗1bJ +δϕ] of Hamc(M,ω) is zero. Since G/Hamc(M,ω) is abelian, the bounded cohomology H2b(G/Hamc(M,ω)) is zero. In particular, the map i∗0: H2b(G) → H2b(Hamc(M,ω)) is injective by (2.2). Moreover, since p: Hamc(M,ω) → Hamc(M,ω) is surjective, the map"
